 "note": [
  "Scripture source: the Indian Revised Version (IRV Hindi, CC BY-SA 4.0), fetched as USX from the ebible mirror (gracious-tech/fetch_collection, bibles/hin_irv/usx), all 66 books. Every mined span was sliced from that text by script, never typed; translators also had an English-phrase search over the whole Bible keyed to the same verse ids for Murray's many uncited quotations.",
  "Translated from the English as the fixture carries it, which already includes the library's BODY_CORRECTIONS for this slug.",
  "Derived by measurement: a row is mined only when the translator reported the quotation verbatim AND the measurement confirms it (a 6+ character quoted segment of that block, or an 8+ character phrase in the chapter, is a byte substring of the cited IRV verse). adapted/self rows and 1 unconfirmed verbatim claim (Luke 18:22, ch05) are self_rendered. Unquoted echoes are not recorded.",
  "KJV/IRV divergences an editor should see: Exod 9:16 'बनाए रखा' (kept alive) for 'raised thee up'; Mark 9:23 has no 'If thou canst believe'; 1 Cor 2:9 blended by Murray with Isa 64:4 (both IRV wordings joined, recorded adapted); Mark 14:30 मुकर जाएगा where Murray argues from the repeated word 'deny' (the other 'deny' quotes use इन्कार); Mark 14:29 ठोकर खाएँ for Murray's 'forsake'; 1 Pet 5:5 no 'be subject'; Ps 62:5 'be silent before God', no 'only'; Gal 3:3 'will you finish in the flesh' where the KJV has 'made perfect' (Murray's own 'perfecting in the flesh' kept outside the quotation); 1 John 4:20 ends as a statement, not a question; Isa 27:2 has no 'red wine' (ch08 follows the KJV sense in prose); Phil 2:13 the full IRV clause includes 'of his good pleasure', which Murray's quotation omits.",
  "Conventions: curly quotation marks mirror the English per chapter (including its unbalanced counts); 'absolute surrender' पूर्ण समर्पण throughout (44×); 'The fruit of the Spirit is love' is the IRV fragment आत्मा का फल प्रेम + है every time (the IRV verse is a verbless list); 'consecration' अर्पण/अर्पित, kept distinct from समर्पण; chapter titles pinned to IRV wording where they quote a verse. The source marks this book's section headings as <p>, not <h2>; kept.",
  "Silent corrections a reviewer should know of (the translator rendered the evident sense, not the English as printed): ch05 block 16 'you could see how you actually could live' — the argument implies 'could not', carried by a rhetorical question; ch09 block 54 'cannot even be used as a pen' rendered as a peg (खूँटी, Ezek 15:3 'pin'); ch09 block 71 'I am His branches' rendered singular.",
  "ENGLISH SOURCE items NOT repaired: ch06 quotes Rom 7:22 as 'law of the Lord' and Rom 8:13 as 'deeds of the flesh' (the KJV and Murray's own other citations have God / body; the Hindi quotes the IRV); ch02 credits 'one heart and one soul' to Acts 2 and 4 (only Acts 4:32); ch07 block 6 appears to have lost a phrase ('and His Spirit'?); ch03 block 43 reads garbled; ch08 'that vineyard or red wine' (Isa 27:2 'a vineyard of red wine'); ch08 Murray's 'one o'clock' for John 4:52's seventh hour, kept.",
  "Two over-long quotations were trimmed in review to what the English actually quotes: ch01 Heb 9:14 ('through the eternal Spirit' — the translator had pasted the rest of the verse into the sentence) and ch01 Rom 7:18 ('there dwelleth no good thing'). ch03's opening <h2> is worded पवित्र आत्मा के निमित्त अलग किए हुए so it does not restate the chapter title — the English heading says 'Holy Ghost' where the title says 'Holy Spirit', a distinction Hindi does not make; the other editions vary it the same way."
